/*!
\mainpage About
\section intro_section Introduction
\tableofcontents

<b>YABIL</b> (Yet Another Big Integer Library) is a lightweight C++ library designed for performing operations on integers of arbitrary size.
The primary goal of this project is to serve research, prototyping, and educational purposes.

If you are looking for a production-grade, high-performance big integer library, you should consider one of the following projects instead:
- [mp++](https://github.com/bluescarni/mppp).
- [GMP (GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library)](https://gmplib.org/).
- [Boost multiprecision](https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_83_0/libs/multiprecision/doc/html/index.html).

\section supported_platforms Supported Platforms

This library is actively build and tested on following configurations:
- Linux - gcc 11 - clang 14
- MacOS - apple-clang 14 
- Windows - MSVC 17
- Android - NDK r26

\section features_section Features

YABIL provides following components:
- \ref yabil::bigint — a core module that offers the @p yabil::bigint::BigInt class for representing and manipulating large integers in the runtime.
- \ref yabil::compile_time - providing @p yabil::compile_time::ConstBigInt - class capable of performing all big integer operations in compile-time.
- \ref yabil::math - containing various math functionalities (e.g. @p yabil::math::pow, @p yabil::math::log).
- \ref yabil::parallel - implementing parallel algorithms for operations on big integers.
- \ref yabil::random - providing simple big integer random number generator.
- \ref yabil::utils - containing useful features, for other parts of library. 

Core functionalities include:
- Support for arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division).
- Bitwise operations (AND, OR, XOR, shifts).
- Comparisons and utility methods.

For list of all features consult documentation of specific namespace.

\section requirements_section Requirements

Core of this library can be build with no additional requirements beyond compiler supporting c++20 standard.

Optionally, this library will use:
- [GTest](https://github.com/google/googletest) - for testing.
- [Google Benchmark](https://github.com/google/benchmark) - for benchmarking.
- [oneTBB](https://github.com/uxlfoundation/oneTBB) - for efficient multithreading (otherwise custom c++ implementation will be used).
- [CUDA](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/) - for custom parallel algorithms, providing performance improvements for very large numbers.   

For instruction on how to enable each of those features see: \ref page_usage.

\section Tutorial

Following pages contain instruction on how to setup and use this library:

- \ref page_usage Usage
- \ref page_examples Examples

